A||||3||qwikgta||Holly TBI for 84-86..why not fit 87-88, Can I make it work anyway.||||5||
Z||000000||qwikgta||05-07-2001||10:31 PM||||I understand that Holly makes an aftermarket type TBI "carb" for the 2.5L motor and it only works with the 84-86 engine.  Why? <P>Can it be modified to work on a 88 2.5, was something changed on the manifold, can you just us a 86 intake or is it in the ECM. What gives.....????  Thanks for any help. <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-08-2001||10:27 AM||||My understanding was that the studs wouldnt fit, becuase of different manifold design.  I dont know if you could get a earlier manifold and make it work with the later block.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Firestarter_87||05-08-2001||11:07 AM||||ummmmmm, I think that all 87-88 DIS Dukes came with a Holley TBI as OEM equipment.  Correct me if I am wrong.<P>Firestarter||||reg||3
Z||000003||theogre||05-08-2001||07:34 PM||||The 87+ 2.5L motor uses a 700 series Delco/Delphi TBI. The entire intake and fuel plumbing are diferant from the older 300 series. Unless you plan significant rework to the linkages, intake, electrical, and fuel line forget it. You'll also need the air cleaner and heatstove setup from the older cars.<P>No, You can't put the older intake manifold on the newer cars. It's been tried.||||reg||1
